---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { Card, CardGrid, LinkCard } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

const banner = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}xtcrash-banner.svg`;
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'XtCrash',
    description:
      'Crash recovery and custom error screens for Android apps. Replace the system crash dialog with a configurable, process-isolated error screen.',
  }}
>
  <img
    src={banner}
    alt="XtCrash — modern crash recovery for Android"
    style="border-radius: 0.25rem; width: 100%; height: auto;"
  />

  <p>
    XtCrash replaces the Android system crash dialog with a configurable error
    screen. A content provider installs an uncaught-exception handler at app
    startup; when a crash happens, the error screen opens in its own process and
    lets the user restart or close the app, review technical details, copy them
    to the clipboard, or share a crash report.
  </p>

  <p>
    The core <code>xtcrash</code> artifact carries no Compose dependency. The
    optional <code>xtcrash-compose</code> artifact adds a drop-in Compose error
    activity and a composable error screen. Applications need Android 6.0
    (API 23) or newer.
  </p>

  <CardGrid>
    <Card title="Process isolation">
      The error screen runs in a dedicated <code>:xtcrash_error</code> process,
      so it still renders after the crashing process dies.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Serializable payload">
      Config, stack trace, and crash metadata travel through the launch intent;
      nothing is held in memory across process boundaries.
    </Card>
    <Card title="No network">
      Reports are assembled on device and shared through Android share intents.
      The library does not send data anywhere on its own.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Handler-chain friendly">
      Initialize XtCrash first, then Crashlytics, ACRA, or another handler. Any
      previously installed uncaught-exception handler is preserved.
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>Start here</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="/XtCrash/quickstart/">Quick start</a>: install, configure, and
      trigger a first test crash.</li>
    <li><a href="/XtCrash/configuration/">Configuration</a>: complete
      <code>CrashConfig</code> reference.</li>
    <li><a href="/XtCrash/introduction/">Introduction</a>: artifact map and
      non-goals.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Guides</h2>

  <CardGrid>
    <LinkCard
      title="Custom error screen"
      href="/XtCrash/custom-error-screen/"
      description="Subclass the error activity, register it in the manifest, and use the intent helpers."
    />
    <LinkCard
      title="Jetpack Compose"
      href="/XtCrash/compose/"
      description="Drop-in activity, composable screen, and custom Compose designs."
    />
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>Project links</h2>

  <CardGrid>
    <LinkCard
      title="GitHub repository"
      href="https://github.com/SoufianoDev/XtCrash"
      description="Sources, issues, releases, and build instructions."
    />
    <LinkCard
      title="Contributing"
      href="https://github.com/SoufianoDev/XtCrash/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md"
      description="Development workflow, module layout, and pull-request process."
    />
  </CardGrid>

  <p>
    XtCrash descends from
    <a href="https://github.com/TutorialsAndroid/crashx">CrashX</a>, which itself
    descends from
    <a href="https://github.com/Ereza/CustomActivityOnCrash">CustomActivityOnCrash</a>
    by Eduard Ereza Martínez. The chain is recorded in the repository's
    <code>NOTICE</code> file.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>
